# Publishability: nothing personal and nothing reproducible reaches history.
# The principle: this repository publishes the INSTRUMENTS, not the artifacts of
# applying them to the kit itself. The owner's workshop (spec, build journal,
# audits, plans, handoffs) lives in docs/private/ and never enters git.

# The owner's internal layer: spec, progress, blockers, backlog, decision
# journal, audits, analytical notes, implementation plans, handoffs.
docs/private/

# Session mechanics: the session entry point and the snapshot. Private by
# nature and constantly changing (the .env pattern). Only the template,
# docs/NEW_SESSION_PROMPT.example.md, is committed.
docs/NEW_SESSION_PROMPT.md
docs/.session-current.md

# Eval artifacts (module 11): scorecards and baseline; they carry usage counters
# derived from private transcripts. Reproducible with eval.sh.
docs/evals/

# Consolidation raw material and drafts (module 12): private transcripts and
# snapshots. Reproducible with consolidate.sh; the owner merges the accepted
# distillate by hand.
docs/consolidation/

# Local Claude Code settings and Telegram bridge uploads.
.claude/settings.local.json
.ccgram-uploads/

# Translated versions of the architecture visualization - the owner's local
# layer, reproducible (see the /arch-viz command). English is canonical.
docs/arch/*.ru.json
docs/arch/*.ru.html
